stnsd serves users, groups and their SSH public keys over the STNS v1 HTTP
API, reading them from a TOML file.  Clients resolve accounts against it
through nsswitch, and sshd fetches authorized keys from it.

It is a second implementation of the API upstream STNS defines, in C and with
no dependency beyond libc, for machines where the Go server is inconvenient or
impossible -- which on NetBSD includes every port Go has never been taught.
The configuration file is the same one, and a test suite serves the same file
from both servers and compares every answer.

Only the TOML backend is implemented: no LDAP, no Redis, no etcd, and no TLS
of its own.
